Package: bilatr
Title: Hierarchical Dynamic IRT Models for Dyadic Conflict Trajectories
Version: 0.9.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Randahl", , "david.randahl@fhs.se", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Magnus", "Lundgren", role = "aut"),
    person("Carl", "Vikberg", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Fits a hierarchical Bayesian dynamic item-response-theory-style
    model to dyadic event data in order to estimate latent conflict
    trajectories. Users supply CAMEO-coded (or any categorically coded)
    dyadic event data in a documented, validated format; action types
    discriminate between high- and low-conflict states through a
    Dirichlet-multinomial likelihood, and dyad-specific latent states
    follow a random-walk process, with support for both single-dyad
    time-series and multi-dyad panel estimation. Includes GDELT
    download/ingest helpers and a CAMEO recoding table, 'cmdstanr'-based
    fitting wrappers, and tidy posterior extraction utilities.
